exam: It is given that a library held {n} volumes, subsequently acquired {m} further volumes and thereafter donated {k} volumes to a school. Determine the number of volumes presently held.
exam: Whereas the enrolment of a school stood at {n.words} pupils, and in September {m} pupils were admitted and {k} pupils departed, ascertain the present enrolment.
exam: A farm maintained {n} hens; the proprietor purchased {m} hens and disposed of {k} hens by sale. State the number of hens presently kept.
exam: Compute the result of increasing {n} by {m} and diminishing the sum by {k}.
exercise: A library had {n} books. When old Mr Hall passed away, he left it {m} books from his shelves, and the library gave {k} worn books to a school. How many books does the library have now?
exercise: A shop had {n} cans of paint. A delivery of {m} more came, and then {k} cans "fell off the back of a lorry" — they were stolen. How many cans are left in the shop?
test: bloody firm had {n} staff, took on {m} more in spring, then "rightsized" — let {k} go. how many still got a job there
